From fa93d8a1ceadaa7fea60bd6e1e89f2240feaa930 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:32:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(flows): headline a run error by its first line; keep
 the rest in Details

A deep research run whose planner reply could not be parsed showed the whole
2,000-character message (the model's raw reply as JSON) as the run card's red
headline, beside a "The flow stopped:" label squeezed into its own column
(reproduced on develop 2026-11-19 with the server's own execution view). The
headline is now the message's first line, clamped to two lines, under "The
flow hit an error" for a flow_error. Details gains the error type and the full
message in a scrolling block, and says how many characters the record cut when
the server reports message_truncated_chars.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BHQAws7LSR8fWEJvjbJM4q
